WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
[Unknown Male Voice] There's no doubting what you've achieved on a technical level.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.280
these are clearly state of the art.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:12.060
There are just certain... design choices that were made for these robots...

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.220
that we don't fully understand.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.660
We were hoping that you could shed some light on those.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.000
[Mr. Afton] She can dance...

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.140
she can sing...

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.760
She's equipped with a built-in helium tank for inflating balloons right at her finger tips...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.140
She can take song requests...

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.540
she can even dispense ice cream.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.760
[First Male Voice] With all due respect, those aren't the design choices we were curious about, Mr. Afton.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
*Main Menu Song (Gradual Liquidation) plays.*

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.600
[Mark] Mr. Afton?

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.320
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier and welcome back to Five Nights at Freddy's

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.220
Now we're in a Sister Location.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.040
Which means that we're not in a Freddy Fazbear's Pizzeria,

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.500
and that introduction was interesting because

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.460
we just got introduced to two new characters

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.140
we've never heard from before

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.140
or at least that's what I'm assuming because

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.140
that definitely wasn't Phone Guy

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.520
and the other guy, Mr. Afton...

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.660
seems to be the designer of, at least, these animatronics.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.460
Now, in my mind, I'm wondering if this guy designed ALL the animatronics

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.500
But I'm not 100% sure about that because these guys are definitely--

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.160
ew--

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.040
Definitely, from a fundamental standpoint, different than the previous animatronics

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.460
So, honestly who knows!

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.000
We don't know anything at this point.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
So Im'ma stop theorizing...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.500
I'm gonna stop assuming anything about this game, because I don't know a damn thing,

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.220
and we're gonna get right into the meat of this story,

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.580
right now.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.480
So-uh-I wanna thank Scott for uh giving me early access to-

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.820
[Little Girl Voice] Daddy? Why won't you let me play with her?

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.620
*Faint Garbled Noise*

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.660
[Mark] Did you hear words there?

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.960
[Robotic Male Voice] Welcome to the first day to your exciting new career!

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:53.680
[Mark] Hi!

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.140
[Robotic Male Voice] Whether you were approached at a job fair, read our ad in 'Screws, Bolts, and Hairpins',

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.160
or if this is the result of a dare, we welcome you.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.140
I will be your personal guide to help you get started.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.940
I'm a model 5 of the Handyman's Robotics and Unit Repair System,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.140
but you can call me Hand Unit.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.380
[Mark, whispering] Hand Unit?
[Hand Unit] Your new career promises challenge,

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:15.800
intrigue, and endless janitorial opportunities.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:16.980
*Sudden Loud Click* 
Please enter your name as seen above.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.580
[Mark] Jesus!
*Loud Click* 
[Hand Unit] Please enter your name as seen

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.180
[Hand Unit] above the keypad.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:19.680
[Mark] Oh, okay!

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.680
[Hand Unit] This cannot be changed later, so please be careful!

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.680
[Mark] Wait, is my name Mike?

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.560
Do I have to enter that name?

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.260
I mean- okay, wait a minute.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.340
Mike, as in Mike Schmidt?!

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.580
Because, Mike Schmidt was the first guy from the first Five Nights at Freddy's

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.360
and I'm not 100% sure that was that...

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.840
I dunno if I can hit this.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.340
HE-BEHP!

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.380
I think I got it!

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.640
M, A--

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.140
Beeh!

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.000
No, no...

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Oh... where's R-- I can't read this--

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:43.500
HA!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.960
Ahhh...

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:45.460
HA!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.180
Aw, shit.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.380
[Hand Unit] It seems that you had some trouble with the keypad.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:48.880
[Mark] No.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.840
[Hand Unit] I see what you were trying to type, and I will autocorrect it for you

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:52.760
One moment.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.980
Welcome, "Eggs Benedict".

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.240
[Mark] What the -laughs- I, I'm not
*Laughing* I- I'm not- I'm not Benedict Cumberbatch

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.100
I'm not Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.680
I'm me! I'm Markiplier!

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.680
Thanks for...entering my name correctly--

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.980
*Loud Beep*
 ..Oh, Jesus

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.020
What the hell is going on here?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.080
Oh, that's so weird.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.140
Ohhh, what is this?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.720
Where am I?

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.780
*Dull button beep*

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.560
Hello?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.560
*Button beeping*

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.740
Is someone gonna let me outta here?

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.080
Am I actually going--
 *Elevator Stops*

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.500
*Cheery jingle plays*

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.260
(Yelling) Ohh!

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.220
Ah! This is cool!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:25.980
Oh, this is really cool.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.840
Now Scott, when he--when he gave me the key,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.620
he said that this game was going to be very diff--

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.960
[Hand Unit] You can now open the elevator, using that bright, red, and obvious button.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.780
[Mark] Oh!

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.780
[Hand Unit] Let's get to work.
[Mark] Okay.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.640
Alright then. HA-BOINK.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.140
*Door Opens*

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.320
Oh boy. Why is it all 'danger'?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.940
Why is it 'danger'?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.000
(Laughing) Wh-Why are going in the 'danger'?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.920
I don't wanna crawl down there.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.840
Okay, let's crawl down there.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.440
[Hand Unit] Allow me to fill this somewhat frightening silence

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.780
with some light-hearted banter.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:56.880
Due to the massive success and, even more so, the unfortunate closing of

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.440
Freddy Fazbear's Pizza, it was clear that the stage was set,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.780
*Thumping from the vents*
[Hand Unit] no pun intended,

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.780
for another contender in children's entertainment.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:10.120
Unlike most entertainment venues, our robotic entertainers are rented out for private parties during the day.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:15.480
And it's your job to get the robots back in proper, working order before the following morning.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.180
You are now in the primary control module.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.440
It's actually a crawl space between the two front show rooms.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.620
Now, let's get started with your daily tasks.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.580
View the window to your left.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.120
[Mark] Uh.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.040
[Hand Unit] This is the Ballora Gallery Party Room and Dance Studio,

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.980
encouraging kids to get fit and enjoy pizza.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.600
Let's turn on the light and see if Ballora is on stage.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.980
Press the blue button on the elevated keypad to your left.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.500
[Mark] I'm trying, man.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:42.560
*Low buzzing* 
Oh.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.080
Where's Ballora?

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.760
[Hand Unit] Uh-oh. It looks like Ballora doesn't feel like dancing.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.620
[Mark] Oh-ho-ho...

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.940
[Hand Unit] Let's give her some motivation.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.180
Press the red button now to administer a controlled shock.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.840
Maybe that will put the spring back in her step.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:55.740
[Mark] What?!

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.660
Why am I gonna make them mad?!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.200
Why do I want Dancey-Pants to be mad at me?! (Right, Mark!!)

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.080
*Loud electrical shock*
[Mark] Aw, geez.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.000
Ballora-
[Hand Unit] Let's check the light again.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.260
[Mark] I don't wanna.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.700
Why are you making me do this?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.200
*click*

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.060
Oh, it's broken.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.180
Oh. Ohh!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.380
Now she's dancing!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.720
[Hand Unit] Excellent. Ballora is feeling like her old self again

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.940
and will be ready to perform again tomorrow.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:23.460
[Mark] Ohhhh.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.520
[Hand Unit] Now, view the window to your right.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.260
[Mark] Oh, okay.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.980
[Hand Unit] This is the Funtime Auditorium, where Funtime Foxy encourages kids to play and share.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.440
Try the light. Let's see what Funtime Foxy is up to.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.080
[Mark] Uh--again. I don't know if I want to.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.060
If I know anything about angering ANY animatronic,

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.320
it's that Foxy

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.480
is a big ol' bag of dicks, (Haha, too funny, Mark!)

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.580
*Low buzzing* 
and hates me.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.360
Ah jeez.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.940
[Hand Unit] Looks like Funtime Foxy is taking the day off.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.440
Let's motivate Funtime Foxy with a controlled shock.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.980
[Mark] Ah. Nothing like a good bit of electro-motivation to get the day started.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.280
Ha-BOOSKIE!
*Loud electrical shock*
Oh, jeez.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.840
Maybe it's like Futurama, and they really like this stuff.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.440
*Low buzzing*
Uh-oh. Uh-oh.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.400
[Hand Unit] Let's try another controlled shock.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.820
[Mark] Mmm- How 'bout we don't?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:15.520
How 'bout we don't? How 'bout we give him a nice cupcake and everyone goes along with their day?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.520
*Loud electrical shock*

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.840
*Low creaking*

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:20.500
Eee!

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.400
*Low buzzing*
Oh, God!

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.380
[Hand Unit] Looks like Funtime Foxey is in perfect working order.
[Mark] Hell yeah.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.480
[Hand Unit] Great job!

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.760
In front of you is another vent shaft.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.900
Crawl through it to reach the Circus Gallery Control Module.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.260
[Mark] I don't want to!

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.400
Why are you making me crawl?!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:43.220
It was--uh--it was--everyone else was supposed to crawl through the vents to kill ME!

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.060
And they're gonna do that.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.180
I've a funny feeling...

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.880
Ohh- Why can I look around here?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.460
Oh. Why do I need to crawl faster?!

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.260
Eeeeuh.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.000
(Groaning) Euugh!

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.820
[Female Computer Voice] Motion Trigger: Circus Gallery Vent.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:02.820
[Mark, yelling] Uwaah!

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.140
Is that me or is that something else?!

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.300
If that's something else,

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:07.340
I'm fucked.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:08.660
If that's me,

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:10.700
uh...

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.060
Okay.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.840
*Metallic clanging noise*
 [Hand Unit] On the other side of the glass--
[Mark] Oh, god--
[Hand Unit] is Circus Baby's Auditorium.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.780
Let's check the light and see what Baby is up to.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.340
[Mark] Maybe we don't! Maybe I should quit this horrible job!

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.800
I mean, I'm literally being talked to by an artificial intelligence.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.580
What era is this in?

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.500
It's like steampunk or electro-punk technology here.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.480
Boink. 
*Low buzzing* 
Oho. She's not there.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:38.740
[Hand Unit] Looks like a few of the lights are out, but we can fix that later.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.920
Let's encourage Baby to cheer up with a controlled shock.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.040
(Mark groans)

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.940
*Loud electrical shock*
[Mark] Eugh!

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:47.640
Something tells me

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.080
angering Baby might be the worst decision.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.540
*Low buzzing*
Not yet!

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.700
[Hand Unit] Let's try another controlled shock.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.480
[Mark] Uh-- Le-let's do that thing.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.180
Oh, there's a lot - there's a lot of beepers and boopers over here!

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.540
I'm gonna beep and bonk my way to Beeptown. (Mark...)

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.460
I can't click on your nose.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.100
You're-- you look like you're dead Balloon Boy over ther-

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.200
That is definitely 100% Balloon Boy over there.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.420
Hee-DOOSKIE!

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.260
*Loud electrical shock*

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.060
Nice!

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.100
Okay...

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:15.940
*Loud buzzing*

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:16.440
Uh-oh.
*Loud buzzing*

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.580
*Low buzzing*

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.720
[Hand Unit] Let's try another controlled shock.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.360
[Mark] Why-- why can't YOU do this?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.260
Why does it have to be a physical button, that way you can place the blame on ME?

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.120
*Loud electrical shock*

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.100
*Low buzzing*

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:29.600
Uh-oh.
*Low buzzing*

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:30.700
*Low buzzing*

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:33.320
[Hand Unit] Great job, Circus Baby! We knew we could count on you.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:33.820
[Mark] Wh-- I--

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.780
[Hand Unit] That concludes your duties for your first night on the job.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.980
We don't want you to leave overwhelmed.

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.940
Otherwise, you might not come back.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:44.960
Please leave using the vent behind you and we'll see you again tomorrow.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.220
[Mark] Wh-I didn't see Baby?!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.200
*Low buzzing*

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.400
I don't see her!
*Low buzzing*

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.260
*low buzzing*

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.020
*Button click*

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:52.820
*Low buzzing*

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.020
Where is she?
*Low buzzing*

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:54.600
*Low buzzing*

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.360
Uh-- Maybe-- maybe I'm just gonna--

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.560
Maybe I'm gonna forget about this and go back.

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.040
Alright. Goodbye.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.960
Oh, man. This is so weird.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.920
Alright. Let's skedaddle on out of here so I--

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:05.980
*Loud metallic thud*

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.940
*Repeated metallic banging*
(Screaming) Augh!

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.080
*Repeated banging*
[Female Computer Voice] Motion Trigger:

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:10.600
*Footsteps*
Circus Gallery Vent

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.960
*Footsteps*

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.320
[Mark, groaning] Eeugh! 
*Footsteps*

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.340
*upbeat music*
*Happy Music* Heyyy!

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.560
Heeeeyyyy!

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:16.980
He-huh!

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.120
Uugh!

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.240
What the fuck was that?! (Baby trying to destroy you)

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.200
*Upbeat music continues*

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.400
Oh, boy!
*Music fades out*

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.740
Enjoy some time at home!

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:25.240
Where-- hah--

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:28.240
Ha-- My nightmares will consume my dreams!

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:35.040
[TV announcer] Another day, another dramatic entry in the lives of Vlad and his distressed mistress.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.320
Where will they go?

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.940
What will they do?

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.260
All of that and more, happening now.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.580
[Vlad] Clara, I tell you: The baby isn't mine.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.080
*Crunch*
[Vlad] Clara, I tell you: The baby isn't mine.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:44.920
[Vlad] Clara, I tell you: The baby isn't mine.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.200
[Clara] Count, I tell you that it is.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:46.860
(Mark laughs)
[Clara] Count, I tell you that it is.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.480
(Mark laughs)
You're the only vampire I've ever loved.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.040
You're the only vampire I've ever loved.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.080
And the baby turns his bottles into powdered milk!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.560
[Vlad] That doesn't mean anything!

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.620
[Clara] He sleeps on the ceiling fan!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.400
[Vlad] Upright, or upside down?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.660
[Clara] What does it matter?

